1. Definitions

  “Software” means the Apiquick source code, binaries, documentation,
  and other materials in this repository.

  “Natural person” means an individual acting in a personal capacity,
  not on behalf of an organization.

  “Legal entity” includes a company, a sole trader acting in a business
  capacity, a public body, and anyone using the Software for, or at the
  expense of, an organization.

  “Permitted purposes” means software testing and software development
  (including API debugging, writing and checking requests, and local
  work with collections).

  “Derivative work” means any modification, fork, port, rewrite,
  patched build, embedding of the Software’s code in another product,
  and any program or service based on the Software, its source code,
  architecture, or a substantial part of it.

2. Royalty-free license for natural persons

  A natural person is granted a worldwide, non-exclusive,
  non-transferable, revocable, royalty-free right to:

  (a) download, install, and run the Software as provided, for personal
      Permitted purposes;
  (b) make copies solely for personal backup, without changing the
      Software’s files.

  This license does not grant any right to modify the Software, create
  Derivative works, or use the Software or its code as the basis of
  another program.

  Personal use means use that is not for an organization’s commercial
  benefit and not as a paid or other business service to third parties.

3. Legal entities — permission required

  A legal entity may not copy, install, run, study for development,
  modify, distribute, or otherwise use the Software unless the Licensor
  gives prior written permission (a contract, letter, license key, or
  other express written instrument of the Licensor).

  To request permission, state the organization, intended use, and a
  contact, in an issue or as the Licensor otherwise directs.

4. Restrictions (unless agreed in writing)

  You may not:

  (a) modify, adapt, or decompile the Software (except to the limited
      extent a mandatory rule of law cannot be waived);
  (b) create Derivative works, forks, or your own clients, services, or
      products based on the Software or its source code;
  (c) copy a substantial part of the Software’s source into another
      project;
  (d) sublicense, sell, rent, or offer the Software as a service (SaaS)
      to third parties;
  (e) remove copyright or license notices;
  (f) claim that the Software is approved, certified, or intended for
      use outside Permitted purposes;
  (g) use the Licensor’s trademarks without separate consent.

  Publication of source code in a repository is not permission to
  create derivatives and does not make the Software open source.

5. Disclaimer

  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
  EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF
